   "evidence": "Moments.lean:36 `def count (obs : X \u2192 S) (\u03c3 : S) : \u2115 := (Finset.univ.filter (fun x => obs x = \u03c3)).card`; variables `{X S ...}` carry no `SignType` constraint; first sign-specific declaration is `inverseCoeff` at l.114. Other repo files already express the same concept ad hoc, e.g. TauCeti/Data/SignType/Cardinality.lean:38 `{i | u i = 0}.ncard`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/RealAlgebraic/SignDetermination/Moments.lean",
   "fix": "Drop the wrapper and state the results directly with Mathlib's idiom `Fintype.card {x // obs x = \u03c3}` / `#{x | obs x = \u03c3}` (Mathlib/Data/Fintype/Card.lean has `Fintype.card_subtype`); if a named definition is really wanted, put it and its two lemmas in a generic `TauCeti/Data/Fintype/` file under `TauCeti`, not `TauCeti.SignDetermination`, and import it here.",
   "issue": "`count`, `count_pos` (l.40) and `count_of_injective` (l.99) are fully generic (any `S` with `DecidableEq`, no signs, no matrices): the fiber cardinality of a finite family. Placing them in `TauCeti.SignDetermination`/Moments.lean hides a broadly useful primitive where no one else in the repo will find it.",
   "line": 36
  }
 ],
